+## Submission retention and idempotency
+
 - [ ] **REC-001**: When an authenticated worker submits a valid visit edit, the system SHALL retain the submitted payload with its visit ID, author ID, and server receipt time.
 - [ ] **REC-002**: When a submission repeats an accepted idempotency key with an identical payload, the system SHALL return the original acceptance result without creating another stored submission.
 - [ ] **REC-003**: When a submission repeats an accepted idempotency key with a different payload, the system SHALL reject the submission and leave the original submission unchanged.
 - [ ] **REC-004**: When edits derived from the same starting visit state are accepted, the system SHALL preserve both original submissions regardless of the concurrency policy's outcome.
+
+## Submission envelope
+
+- [ ] **REC-007**: The system shall require each visit submission to include either a base revision ID that identifies the specific revision the worker edited from, or a null indicator signifying this is the first submission for that visit.
+
+## Revision advancement and competing revisions
+
+- [ ] **REC-008**: When a visit submission names a null base revision ID and no revisions exist for that visit, the system SHALL create the first revision and set it as the visit's current HEAD.
+- [ ] **REC-009**: When a visit submission names a base revision ID that matches the visit's current HEAD revision, the system SHALL create a new revision and advance the HEAD to it.
+- [ ] **REC-010**: When a visit submission names a base revision ID that refers to an existing revision for that visit but does not match the current HEAD, the system SHALL record it as a competing revision and mark the visit as needs-review.
+- [ ] **REC-011**: If a visit submission names a base revision ID that does not refer to any existing revision for that visit, the system SHALL reject the submission.
+
+## Visit status and retrieval
+
 - [ ] **REC-005**: When a caller retrieves a visit, the system SHALL indicate whether unresolved review work exists for that visit.
-- [ ] **REC-006**: When a coordinator resolves review work, the system SHALL retain the coordinator's identity and the contributing submission IDs with the resolution outcome.
+- [ ] **REC-012**: While a visit is needs-review, the system SHALL exclude it from export eligibility.
+
+## Coordinator review and resolution
+
+- [ ] **REC-013**: When a coordinator requests review data for a needs-review visit, the system SHALL return each competing revision's payload, author ID, revision ID, and server receipt time.
+- [ ] **REC-014**: When a coordinator selects a revision to resolve a needs-review visit, the system SHALL advance the visit's HEAD to the selected revision and clear the needs-review status.
+- [ ] **REC-015**: When a coordinator resolves a needs-review visit, the system SHALL retain all competing revisions, including those not selected, permanently in the visit's revision history.
+- [ ] **REC-006**: When a coordinator resolves review work for a visit, the system SHALL retain the coordinator's identity, the selected revision ID, all competing revision IDs considered, and the resolution timestamp.
